        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Walking Pad Not Working", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/walking-pad-not-working/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why is my walking pad not turning on?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually the outlet, the pad's own power switch, or the cord. Test the socket with a lamp, check the rocker switch near the cord, and press in any reset button the manual shows. If it is still dead, it needs the brand's support.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why will my walking pad not start?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Check the safety key or magnet, whether the pad is in standby or child lock, and whether the remote or app is needed to start it. Unplug and check nothing is blocking the belt. A motor that hums without moving the belt needs support.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why is my walking pad remote not working?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Replace the battery first, then re-pair the remote using the sequence in the manual, since pairing is often lost after a power cut. Check line of sight for infrared remotes, and test the pad with its own button or app.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How do I fix a walking pad belt that slips?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Lubricate it as the manual says first, because a dry deck is the usual cause. If it still slips, tighten both rear bolts equally a quarter turn at a time, stopping as soon as the slip stops.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why does my walking pad stop by itself?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "An auto-stop timer, heat from a dry belt or long heavy use, overload from running or exceeding the weight limit, or a shared circuit. Let it cool, lubricate, and check the manual for timer settings.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How do I reset a walking pad?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Switch it off, unplug it for about a minute, plug it back in and switch on. Some models have a reset button or a factory-reset button sequence; follow the manual for yours rather than a generic sequence.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
